{
  "id": "p5",
  "title": "for Loops",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p5-l1",
      "title": "for … to … do",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "for i := 1 to 5 do statement runs the statement 5 times, with i = 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5. The loop variable must be declared, usually as an integer.",
        "For more than one statement in the loop, use begin … end, just like with if.",
        "Pascal counts the steps before the loop starts, so the loop always ends. That's one reason Wirth liked it for teaching."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Count;",
          "var",
          "  i: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  for i := 1 to 5 do",
          "    write(i, ' ');",
          "  writeln;",
          "  for i := 1 to 3 do",
          "  begin",
          "    write('Round ', i);",
          "    writeln(': ', i * i);",
          "  end;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "1 2 3 4 5 ",
          "Round 1: 1",
          "Round 2: 4",
          "Round 3: 9"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p5-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many times does for i := 3 to 7 do … run?",
          "options": [
            "5",
            "4",
            "7",
            "3"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "3, 4, 5, 6 and 7."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Even;",
            "var",
            "  i: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for i := 1 to 4 do",
            "    write(i * 2, ' ');",
            "  writeln;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "2 4 6 8",
            "1 2 3 4",
            "2 4 6 8 10",
            "8"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "i goes from 1 to 4, and each round prints i * 2."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Print the numbers 1 to 10.",
          "code": [
            "  for i := 1 ___ 10 do",
            "    writeln(i);"
          ],
          "options": [
            "to",
            "until",
            "..",
            "upto"
          ],
          "answer": "to",
          "explanation": "for … to … do."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l1-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Loop;",
            "var",
            "  i: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for i := 1 to 3 do",
            "    writeln('Hi');",
            "  writeln('Bye');",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "Hi\nHi\nHi\nBye",
            "Hi\nBye\nHi\nBye\nHi\nBye",
            "Hi\nHi\nHi",
            "Bye"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Without begin … end, only the first writeln is inside the loop."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l1-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Loop;",
            "var",
            "  i: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for i = 1 to 5 do",
            "    writeln(i);",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 4,
          "explanation": "The loop variable gets its start value with := , like any assignment."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What happens with for i := 5 to 1 do …?",
          "options": [
            "The loop doesn't run at all",
            "It counts down",
            "It runs forever",
            "Error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "5 is already bigger than 1. To count down, use downto."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5-l2",
      "title": "downto and Counting",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "downto counts backwards: for i := 10 downto 1 do … ",
        "Loops are great for adding things up: start a sum at 0, and add to it in every round.",
        "The loop variable can also be a char: for c := 'A' to 'Z' do write(c); prints the alphabet."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Sums;",
          "var",
          "  i, sum: integer;",
          "  c: char;",
          "begin",
          "  for i := 5 downto 1 do",
          "    write(i, ' ');",
          "  writeln('Liftoff!');",
          "  sum := 0;",
          "  for i := 1 to 100 do",
          "    sum := sum + i;",
          "  writeln('1 + 2 + ... + 100 = ', sum);",
          "  for c := 'A' to 'F' do",
          "    write(c);",
          "  writeln;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "5 4 3 2 1 Liftoff!",
          "1 + 2 + ... + 100 = 5050",
          "ABCDEF"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p5-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does for i := 3 downto 1 do write(i) print?",
          "options": [
            "321",
            "123",
            "3",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "downto counts down."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l2-e2",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Count down from 10.",
          "code": [
            "  for i := 10 ___ 1 do",
            "    writeln(i);"
          ],
          "options": [
            "downto",
            "to",
            "down",
            "-1"
          ],
          "answer": "downto",
          "explanation": "downto instead of to."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Add;",
            "var",
            "  i, s: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  s := 0;",
            "  for i := 1 to 5 do",
            "    s := s + i;",
            "  writeln(s);",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "15",
            "5",
            "10",
            "0"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 = 15."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l2-e4",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program should print 6 (1 + 2 + 3), but it prints 3. Which line is in the wrong place?",
          "code": [
            "program Sum;",
            "var",
            "  i, s: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for i := 1 to 3 do",
            "  begin",
            "    s := 0;",
            "    s := s + i;",
            "  end;",
            "  writeln(s);",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 6,
          "explanation": "s := 0 belongs before the loop. Inside it, the sum starts over in every round."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Abc;",
            "var",
            "  c: char;",
            "begin",
            "  for c := 'a' to 'e' do",
            "    write(c);",
            "  writeln;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "abcde",
            "ABCDE",
            "a b c d e",
            "12345"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A char loop goes through the letters."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l2-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which loop prints every second number from 2 to 10?",
          "options": [
            "for i := 1 to 5 do write(i * 2, ' ')",
            "for i := 2 to 10 step 2 do",
            "for i := 2 to 10 do i := i + 1",
            "for i := 10 downto 2 do"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Pascal's for has no step: count normally and calculate the value."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5-l3",
      "title": "Loops in Loops",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A loop inside a loop runs completely in every round of the outer one. That's how you make tables and patterns.",
        "Use different loop variables for the two loops, like row and col.",
        "Width formatting (x:4) keeps the columns of a table straight."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Table;",
          "var",
          "  row, col: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  for row := 1 to 4 do",
          "  begin",
          "    for col := 1 to 4 do",
          "      write(row * col:4);",
          "    writeln;",
          "  end;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "   1   2   3   4",
          "   2   4   6   8",
          "   3   6   9  12",
          "   4   8  12  16"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p5-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many stars does this print? for a := 1 to 3 do for b := 1 to 4 do write('*')",
          "options": [
            "12",
            "7",
            "4",
            "3"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "4 stars in each of the 3 rounds."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Tri;",
            "var",
            "  row, k: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for row := 1 to 3 do",
            "  begin",
            "    for k := 1 to row do",
            "      write('*');",
            "    writeln;",
            "  end;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "*\n**\n***",
            "***\n***\n***",
            "***\n**\n*",
            "******"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The inner loop runs row times."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l3-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Print each value in 4 columns.",
          "code": [
            "    write(row * col___);"
          ],
          "options": [
            ":4",
            ":0:4",
            "%4",
            ",4"
          ],
          "answer": ":4",
          "explanation": ":4 right-aligns in 4 columns."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l3-e4",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program prints only one long line instead of a table. Which line is in the wrong place?",
          "code": [
            "program Grid;",
            "var",
            "  r, c: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  for r := 1 to 3 do",
            "  begin",
            "    for c := 1 to 3 do",
            "    write(r * c:3);",
            "  end;",
            "  writeln;",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 9,
          "explanation": "The writeln must be inside the outer loop (before end;), so every row ends with a line break."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l3-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why do the two loops need different variables?",
          "options": [
            "The inner loop would change the outer loop's counter",
            "Pascal forbids the same name twice in a program",
            "For speed",
            "They don't"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Each loop needs its own counter."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-l3-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the lines in order: print 3 rows of 5 dots.",
          "lines": [
            "for r := 1 to 3 do",
            "begin",
            "  for c := 1 to 5 do",
            "    write('.');",
            "  writeln;",
            "end;"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "for r := 1 to 3 do",
            "begin",
            "  for c := 1 to 5 do",
            "    write('.');",
            "  writeln;",
            "end;"
          ],
          "explanation": "Outer loop, begin, inner loop with its statement, writeln, end."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
